# Transport Stack Hackathon 2026 — October 2026 data

Two datasets for Delhi buses, covering 1–31 October 2026.

| File | What it is | Size |
|---|---|---:|
| `delhi-dtc-bus-gtfs-rt-2026-10.7z` | Bus GPS: decoded GTFS-Realtime vehicle positions for DTC buses. 31 daily SQLite databases. | 16.1 GB (124 GB unpacked) |
| `October-Delhi.csv.zip` | Bus e-ticketing records (ONDC). One CSV, about 2.56 million tickets. | 66 MB (290 MB unpacked) |
| `SHA256SUMS` | Checksums to verify your downloads. | |

Large downloads can drop. Use a client that resumes, for example `curl -C - -O <url>`.

Verify:

```bash
shasum -a 256 -c SHA256SUMS
```

## Bus GPS (`delhi-dtc-bus-gtfs-rt-2026-10.7z`)

The archive holds one SQLite database per day, named `bus_movements_YYYY_MM_DD.db`. It is non-solid, so you can extract a single day:

```bash
7z l delhi-dtc-bus-gtfs-rt-2026-10.7z                         # list days
7z x delhi-dtc-bus-gtfs-rt-2026-10.7z bus_movements_2026_10_15.db
```

Each database has one table:

```sql
CREATE TABLE vehicle_feed (
  vehicle_id TEXT,  -- bus registration, e.g. DL1PD8979
  lat        TEXT,  -- latitude (WGS84), stored as text
  lng        TEXT,  -- longitude (WGS84), stored as text
  speed      REAL,  -- speed as reported by the feed
  route_id   REAL,  -- route identifier, stored as a float
  trip_id    TEXT,  -- trip identifier assigned by the Transport Stack pipeline
  timestamp  TEXT,  -- observation time, Unix epoch seconds (UTC)
  date       DATE,  -- date (IST)
  time       TEXT   -- clock time (IST)
);
```

DTC buses only. The databases have no indexes; add your own if you need them. The feed is raw: expect duplicates, gaps and GPS noise.

## Ticketing (`October-Delhi.csv.zip`)

One CSV with these columns:

| Column | Example |
|---|---|
| `passenger_count` | `1` |
| `amount` | `"22"` |
| `vehicle_number` | `DL1PD6826` (blank, `NULL`, on about half the rows) |
| `ticket_type_id` | `1` |
| `end_stop_name` | `Mahamaya Flyover West` |
| `route` | `8UP` |
| `start_stop_name` | `Ali Village` |
| `created_at` | `2026-10-28 10:19:18.780611+05:30` |
| `is_ac` | `True` |

## Static GTFS

Routes, stops and schedules for Delhi buses are available from Transport Stack at https://delhi.transportstack.in.

## Source

Transport Stack / IIIT Delhi. Bus GPS is derived from the DTC bus AVL feed. Ticketing is from ONDC e-ticketing.

